<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hoton Nor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1731</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Khoton Nor · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungar-qing-wars">Dzungar–Qing Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hoton Nor was fought in the summer of 1731 near the lake of that name in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, between the Dzungar Khanate and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> forces sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galdan-tseren">Galdan Tseren</a> lured a Qing army under the general Furdan into an ambush and destroyed most of it, one of the heaviest Qing defeats of the period. The Dzungars were checked the following year near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdene-zuu">Erdene Zuu</a>, and peace was made in 1739.</p></div>
